FP16 -> integer conversions returned 0 for every denormal, ignoring the rounding mode

f16_to_i16, f16_to_i32, f16_to_i64, f16_to_ui16, f16_to_ui32 and f16_to_ui64
returned 0 for a denormal input before rounding (raising only inexact). A
denormal FP16 is nonzero and below 0.5, so under round-up +2^-24 must give 1,
and under round-down -2^-24 must give -1 (signed) or integer indefinite with
the invalid flag (unsigned). This affected VCVTSH2SI, VCVTSH2USI,
VCVTPH2[U]W, VCVTPH2[U]DQ and VCVTPH2[U]QQ under embedded rounding and under
MXCSR.RC alike; the truncating forms (the _r_minMag functions) and the i8/ui8
conversions were right.

A denormal now goes to softfloat_roundTo* with its fraction as the fixed-point
significand, as Berkeley SoftFloat 3e does: that value is below 0.25 in the
rounding routines' 12-fraction-bit format, the same side of every rounding
boundary as the true value, so sign, rounding and flags come out right. The
DAZ early return is kept.

Fixed in softfloat3e/f16_to_{i,ui}{16,32,64}.cc. Found 2026-09-29; upstream
master has the same code.

diff --git a/cpu/softfloat3e/f16_to_i16.cc b/cpu/softfloat3e/f16_to_i16.cc
index 3b3897b..ef97a39 100644
--- a/cpu/softfloat3e/f16_to_i16.cc
+++ b/cpu/softfloat3e/f16_to_i16.cc
@@ -62,16 +62,10 @@ int16_t f16_to_i16(float16 a, uint8_t roundingMode, bool exact, struct softfloat
     }
     /*------------------------------------------------------------------------
     *------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
-    if (! exp) {
-        if (softfloat_denormalsAreZeros(status)) return 0;
-        if (exact && frac) {
-            softfloat_raiseFlags(status, softfloat_flag_inexact);
-        }
-        return 0;
-    }
+    if (! exp && softfloat_denormalsAreZeros(status)) return 0;
     /*------------------------------------------------------------------------
     *------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
-    sig32 = frac | 0x0400;
+    sig32 = exp ? (frac | 0x0400) : frac;
     shiftDist = exp - 0x19;
     if (0 <= shiftDist) {
         sig32 <<= shiftDist;
